#[chapter/03/lore]{
  notes: [
    "The Off-Season Genie is a retired Discount Genie who liquidated his practice: grandiose wishes turned out to be cheap magic, and small honest wishes the expensive kind. The egg is the las..."
    "Wish-physics is karmic momentum: a wish doesn't create from nothing, it redirects momentum reality already has. Perfect version costs a miracle; mediocre version costs one coincidence and..."
    "The Genie can grant anything except see what Boof wants — her want sits below the resolution of instruments built for emperors. The low ambition fascinates him, and he joins the walk."
    "Two old routes wanting one turn settle for free under a traveler who asks nothing grander than a way through. The Genie recognizes his own trade performed by weather."
    "Salt-whales move under the flats; the flats are the roof of their road, and the glowing old routes are whale-roads. Salt-rakers do not stamp on the roof. Two whale-roads that wanted the s..."
    "Signal-skinks bask on a ring of black signal stones around the old signpost and flick their tails in a code only the stones answer, each stone ticking warm in reply. When Boof's shadow cr..."
    "The Genie's instruments have names: the wish-scale, balanced against small stamped brass coincidences; the resolution glass, which shows only wants larger than a loaf; and the want-needle..."
    "The bottle-desk folds out of the Genie's bottle leg by leg: baize top, pigeonholes, a dry inkwell, and one drawer labelled Thursdays that he never lets anyone count. What escapes it smell..."
  ]
}

